PARLIAMENT O
F PAKISTAN
ORDERS OF THE DAYfor the meetinS of the Mailis-e-shoora (Parliament) in joint sitting to be held on Tuesday, the2nd December, 2025 at 11.00 a.m.l. Titowot, Hodith, Noot and national anthem'LEGISTATIVE BUSINESS2. SENATOR AZAM NAZEER TARAR, Minister for Law and Justice and Human Rights' to move that theBill to provide for constitution of a National Commission for Minorities Rights [The National commissionfor Minorities Rights Bill, 20251, as passed by the Majlis-e-shoora (Parliament) and returned by thePresident, be taken into consideration at once under clause (2) of Article 75 of the constitution of thelslamic Republic of Pakista n.[Amendments in a separate list to be moved]
3. SENATOR AZAM NAZEER TARAR, Minister for Law and Justice and Human Rights, to move that theBill to provide for constitution of a National Commission for Minorities Rights [The National Commissionfor Minorities Rights Bill,2025l, be passed.4. syED NAVEED QAMAR, MNA, to move that the Bill further to amend the National Assemblysecretariat Employees Act, 2018 [The National Assembly secretariat Employees (Amendment) Bill, 2025],as passed by the Majlis-e-Shoora (Parliament) and returned by the President, be taken into considerationat once under clause (2) of Article 75 of the constltution of the lslamic Republic of Pakistan'
5. SYED NAVEED CI,AMAR, MNA, to move that the Bill further to amend the National Assemblysecretariat Employees Act, 2018 [The National Assembly secretariat Employees (Amendment) Bill, 2025],be passed.5. SENATOR MOHAMMAD ISHAQ DA& Minister for Foreign Affairs / Deputy Prime Minister' to movethat the Bill to give effect to the convention on the Prohibition of the Development, Production andstockpiling of Bicteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weapons and on their Destruction, 1972 [TheBiological and Toxin weapons convention (lm plementationl }il,20241, as passed by the Majlis-e-shoora(earliiment) and returned by the President, be taken into consideration at once under clause (2) of Article75 of the Constitution of the lslamic Republic of Pakistan.[Amendments in a separate list to be moved]7. SENATOR MOHAMMAO tSHAq DAR, Minister for Foreign Affairs / Deputy Prime Minister, to movethat the Bill to give effect to the convention on the Prohibition of the Development, Production andStockpiling of Baiteriological (Biologica l) and Toxin wea pons and on their Destruction, 7972 lrhe Biologica Iand Toxin Weapons Convention (lmplementation) Bill, 20241, be passed'
8. M5. HUMA AKHTER CHUGHTA|, MNA, to move that the Bill to provide for the establishment of thepakistan lnstitute of Management, sciences and Technology [The Pakistan lnstitute of Management,Sciences and Technology Bill, 20231, as passed by the Majlis-e-Shoora (Parliament) and returned by thePresident, be taken into consideration at once under clause (2) of Article 75 of the constitution of thelsla mic Republic of Pakistan.
[Amendments in a separate list to be moved]

